      "content": "Thanks for this. It's a good start, clear and covers the basics.\n\nI just ran it through the pre-submission audit tool we discussed, and the jargon density score came back a bit lower than I was hoping for. It’s okay, but it might not pass the first automated gate if the density isn't higher. \n\nCould you try a second draft? I really need you to beef up the technical nomenclature and the sophistication of the descriptions to get that score up. Just please, like I said before, don't let it become unreadable or lose the actual scientific logic. We need it to be dense, but it still has to be a real methodology. Try to make it sound even more specialized.",
